[ar:Slim Dusty]
[al:The Very Best Of Slim Dusty]
[ti:Cunnamulla Fella]
[00:03.87] Now I'm a scrubber, runner and a breaker too
[00:07.65] I live on damper and wallaby stew
[00:10.50] I've got a big cattle dog with a staghound cross
[00:14.23] I never saw the scrubber we couldn't toss
[00:17.14] 'Cause I'm the Feller from Cunnamulla
[00:20.66] Yes I'm the Cunnamulla Feller
[00:27.39] Now once when I was drovin' on the cattle trails
[00:30.98] I met a little girl her name was Ada Vale
[00:34.01] I said "Marry me Ada and I'll be the feller
[00:37.50] And we'll settle down in Augathella"
[00:41.36] I'll be the Feller at Augathella
[00:44.84] Yes I'll be the Augathella Feller
[00:51.39] Oh, she said her daddy's name was Charley Ville
[00:55.09] She had a lot of kiddies and a lot of bills
[00:58.23] So I grabbed my horse that was nice and handy
[01:01.60] And I never stopped till I reached Dirranbandi
[01:05.56] I was the dandy at Dirranbandi
[01:09.09] Yes I was the Dirranbandi Dandy
[01:15.58] Now in my moleskin trousers and my Williams boots
[01:19.49] Aboard an outlaw as he leaves the chutes
[01:22.54] In my goose neck spurs I rake their fiery hide
[01:25.90] And the girls all shouting around the ringside
[01:29.11] Oh he's the Feller from Cunnamulla
[01:32.69] Yeah he's the Cunnamulla Feller
[01:39.21] Now I've done a little fightin' in the western bars
[01:43.12] Done a little lovin' neath the moon and stars
[01:46.30] I wear bright clothes and shirts full of colour
[01:49.53] And the girls know me as that certain feller
[01:53.55] Yes he's the Feller from Cunnamulla
[01:57.10] Yes he's the Cunnamulla Feller
[02:00.52] Oh he's the Cunnamulla Feller
[02:03.82] Yes he's the Cunnamulla Feller
